{
  "Joshua.10.12.3-c.html": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/strict.dtd\"><HTML>\n<!-- \n     Computer generated from NoteMaker[20 Jan 2026]: \n     Changes file: 2022.10.19 - Changes.xml, date: 2022.07.03, number: 8 .\n     Remove this token \"****COMPUTER-GENERATED****\" if you edit this file manually.\n-->\n<head><meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\"/>\n  <title>Joshua 10:12.3</title>\n</head>\n<body background=\"../../Images/Background\">\n  <h1>Joshua 10:12.3</h1>\n  <h2>Change patah under ayin to qamats. Add 'c' note.</h2>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"5pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>\n          <img src=\"../../Changes/2022.10.19 - Changes/images/2022.07.03/8-Detail.jpg\"  border=\"4pt\">\n          </img>\n        </center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>Credit: Sefaria.org.</center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n  <p>\n                   The LC's qamats on the ayin is effectively a \"furtive\" qamats. \n               </p>\n  <p>\n                   The Miqra According to the Masorah (MAM) has a patah under the ayin.\n               </p>\n  <p>\n    <b>\n      <i>Daniel Holman</i>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <p align=\"right\">\n    <b><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Changes/2022.10.19 - Changes/2022.10.19 - Changes.xml?2022.07.03-8\">2022.10.19 - Changes.xml : 2022.07.03-8</a>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"20pt\"  border=\"1pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml?c\">All \"Text is correct relative to LC. Usually this marks a peculiarity of the LC relative to the other Masoretic texts.\" ('c') notes</a></center>\n        </p>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml\">Note index</a></center>\n        </p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n</body></HTML>",
  "Joshua.10.24.19-y.html": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/strict.dtd\"><HTML>\n<!-- \n     Computer generated from NoteMaker[20 Jan 2026]: \n     Changes file: 2024.10.19 - Changes.xml, date: 2024.07.08, number: 2 .\n     Remove this token \"****COMPUTER-GENERATED****\" if you edit this file manually.\n-->\n<head><meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\"/>\n  <title>Joshua 10:24.19</title>\n</head>\n<body background=\"../../Images/Background\">\n  <h1>Joshua 10:24.19</h1>\n  <h2>Add transcription note 'y' to yatir ketiv word. (yatir aleph)</h2>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"5pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>\n          <img src=\"../../Changes/2024.10.19 - Changes/images/2024.07.08/2-Detail.jpg\"  border=\"4pt\">\n          </img>\n        </center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>Credit: Sefaria.org.</center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n  <p>The yatir marking for this word is in the left margin; it is a yatir aleph. This word is not represented by a qere/ketiv pair in previous versions of the UXLC or in WLC 4.20.</p>\n  <p>BHL has no qere/ketiv marking and has a final aleph on this word.  BHLA has no entry for this verse.</p>\n  <p>\n    <b>\n      <i>CVK</i>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <p align=\"right\">\n    <b><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Changes/2024.10.19 - Changes/2024.10.19 - Changes.xml?2024.07.08-2\">2024.10.19 - Changes.xml : 2024.07.08-2</a>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"20pt\"  border=\"1pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml?y\">All \"Yatir: The preceding Hebrew letter is \"superfluous\".\" ('y') notes</a></center>\n        </p>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml\">Note index</a></center>\n        </p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n</body></HTML>",
  "Joshua.14.10.4-m.html": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/strict.dtd\"><HTML>\n<!-- \n     Computer generated from NoteMaker[20 Jan 2026]: \n     Changes file: 2023.10.19 - Changes.xml, date: 2023.06.15, number: 1 .\n     Remove this token \"****COMPUTER-GENERATED****\" if you edit this file manually.\n-->\n<head><meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\"/>\n  <title>Joshua 14:10.4</title>\n</head>\n<body background=\"../../Images/Background\">\n  <h1>Joshua 14:10.4</h1>\n  <h2>Change munah under vav to meteg. Add note 'm'.</h2>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"5pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>\n          <img src=\"../../Changes/2023.10.19 - Changes/images/2023.06.15/1-Detail.jpg\"  border=\"4pt\">\n          </img>\n        </center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>Credit: Sefaria.org.</center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n  <p>Both the Aleppo Codex and BHL have a merkha under the vav. The accent under the vav lacks the northeast-to-southwest inclination for transcription as a merkha. Hence, a transcription note 'm' is added.</p>\n  <p>BHL has a merkha under the vav.  BHLA has no entry for this verse.</p>\n  <p>\n    <b>\n      <i>Daniel Holman</i>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <p align=\"right\">\n    <b><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Changes/2023.10.19 - Changes/2023.10.19 - Changes.xml?2023.06.15-1\">2023.10.19 - Changes.xml : 2023.06.15-1</a>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"20pt\"  border=\"1pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml?m\">All \"This meteg is a merkha in other texts.\" ('m') notes</a></center>\n        </p>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml\">Note index</a></center>\n        </p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n</body></HTML>",
  "Joshua.15.10.3-t.html": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/strict.dtd\"><HTML>\n<!-- \n     Computer generated from NoteMaker[20 Jan 2026]: \n     Changes file: 2022.10.19 - Changes.xml, date: 2022.07.03, number: 13 .\n     Remove this token \"****COMPUTER-GENERATED****\" if you edit this file manually.\n-->\n<head><meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\"/>\n  <title>Joshua 15:10.3</title>\n</head>\n<body background=\"../../Images/Background\">\n  <h1>Joshua 15:10.3</h1>\n  <h2>Possible dagesh in he. Add note 't'.</h2>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"5pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>\n          <img src=\"../../Changes/2022.10.19 - Changes/images/2022.07.03/13-Detail.jpg\"  border=\"4pt\">\n          </img>\n        </center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>Credit: Sefaria.org.</center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n  <p>\n                    The dagesh is well-shaped and well-positioned, but faint. It is not expected here.\n               </p>\n  <p>\n                    The Miqra According to the Masorah (MAM) has no dagesh on the he.\n               </p>\n  <p>\n    <b>\n      <i>Daniel Holman</i>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <p align=\"right\">\n    <b><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Changes/2022.10.19 - Changes/2022.10.19 - Changes.xml?2022.07.03-13\">2022.10.19 - Changes.xml : 2022.07.03-13</a>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"20pt\"  border=\"1pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml?t\">All \"Transcription uncertain\" ('t') notes</a></center>\n        </p>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml\">Note index</a></center>\n        </p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n</body></HTML>",
  "Joshua.17.8.9-t.html": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/strict.dtd\"><HTML>\n<!-- \n     Computer generated from NoteMaker[20 Jan 2026]: \n     Changes file: 2022.10.19 - Changes.xml, date: 2022.07.03, number: 14 .\n     Remove this token \"****COMPUTER-GENERATED****\" if you edit this file manually.\n-->\n<head><meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\"/>\n  <title>Joshua 17:8.9</title>\n</head>\n<body background=\"../../Images/Background\">\n  <h1>Joshua 17:8.9</h1>\n  <h2>Possible dagesh in bet. Add note 't'.</h2>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"5pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>\n          <img src=\"../../Changes/2022.10.19 - Changes/images/2022.07.03/14-Detail.jpg\"  border=\"4pt\">\n          </img>\n        </center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>Credit: Sefaria.org.</center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n  <p>\n                    The dagesh is well-shaped but a little low and faint. \n               </p>\n  <p>\n                    The Miqra According to the Masorah (MAM) has no dagesh on the bet.\n               </p>\n  <p>\n    <b>\n      <i>Daniel Holman</i>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <p align=\"right\">\n    <b><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Changes/2022.10.19 - Changes/2022.10.19 - Changes.xml?2022.07.03-14\">2022.10.19 - Changes.xml : 2022.07.03-14</a>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"20pt\"  border=\"1pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml?t\">All \"Transcription uncertain\" ('t') notes</a></center>\n        </p>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml\">Note index</a></center>\n        </p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n</body></HTML>",
  "Joshua.2.1.2-t.html": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/strict.dtd\"><HTML>\n<!-- \n     Computer generated from NoteMaker[20 Jan 2026]: \n     Changes file: 2022.10.19 - Changes.xml, date: 2022.07.03, number: 1 .\n     Remove this token \"****COMPUTER-GENERATED****\" if you edit this file manually.\n-->\n<head><meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\"/>\n  <title>Joshua 2:1.2</title>\n</head>\n<body background=\"../../Images/Background\">\n  <h1>Joshua 2:1.2</h1>\n  <h2>Change sheva under yod to hiriq; change munah on shin to meteg. Add note 't'.</h2>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"5pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>\n          <img src=\"../../Changes/2022.10.19 - Changes/images/2022.07.03/1-Detail.jpg\"  border=\"4pt\">\n          </img>\n        </center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>Credit: Sefaria.org.</center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n  <p>\n                   The text of this word is of poor quality. \n                   Although the usual spelling of Joshua has a sheva under the yod, the LC has only one dot under the yod.\n                   The shuruq under the shin is unclear;\n                       the other mark under the shin is a meteg.\n                   The furtive patah for the ayin is too advanced.\n               </p>\n  <p>\n                    The Miqra According to the Masorah (MAM) has a sheva under the yod and a meteg under the shin.\n               </p>\n  <p>\n    <b>\n      <i>Daniel Holman</i>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <p align=\"right\">\n    <b><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Changes/2022.10.19 - Changes/2022.10.19 - Changes.xml?2022.07.03-1\">2022.10.19 - Changes.xml : 2022.07.03-1</a>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"20pt\"  border=\"1pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml?t\">All \"Transcription uncertain\" ('t') notes</a></center>\n        </p>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml\">Note index</a></center>\n        </p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n</body></HTML>",
  "Joshua.2.1.3-c.html": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/strict.dtd\"><HTML>\n<!-- \n     Computer generated from NoteMaker[20 Jan 2026]: \n     Changes file: 2022.10.19 - Changes.xml, date: 2022.07.03, number: 2 .\n     Remove this token \"****COMPUTER-GENERATED****\" if you edit this file manually.\n-->\n<head><meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\"/>\n  <title>Joshua 2:1.3</title>\n</head>\n<body background=\"../../Images/Background\">\n  <h1>Joshua 2:1.3</h1>\n  <h2>Remove maqaf from end of word. Add note 'c'.</h2>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"5pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>\n          <img src=\"../../Changes/2022.10.19 - Changes/images/2022.07.03/2-Detail.jpg\"  border=\"4pt\">\n          </img>\n        </center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>Credit: Sefaria.org.</center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n  <p>\n                    A maqaf is expected at end of word.\n               </p>\n  <p>\n                    The Miqra According to the Masorah (MAM) has a maqaf at end of word.\n               </p>\n  <p>\n    <b>\n      <i>Daniel Holman</i>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <p align=\"right\">\n    <b><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Changes/2022.10.19 - Changes/2022.10.19 - Changes.xml?2022.07.03-2\">2022.10.19 - Changes.xml : 2022.07.03-2</a>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"20pt\"  border=\"1pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml?c\">All \"Text is correct relative to LC. Usually this marks a peculiarity of the LC relative to the other Masoretic texts.\" ('c') notes</a></center>\n        </p>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml\">Note index</a></center>\n        </p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n</body></HTML>",
  "Joshua.20.4.12-c.html": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/strict.dtd\"><HTML>\n<!-- \n     Computer generated from NoteMaker[20 Jan 2026]: \n     Changes file: 2022.10.19 - Changes.xml, date: 2022.07.03, number: 18 .\n     Remove this token \"****COMPUTER-GENERATED****\" if you edit this file manually.\n-->\n<head><meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\"/>\n  <title>Joshua 20:4.12</title>\n</head>\n<body background=\"../../Images/Background\">\n  <h1>Joshua 20:4.12</h1>\n  <h2>Accent on nun is a merkha. Add note 'c'</h2>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"5pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>\n          <img src=\"../../Changes/2022.10.19 - Changes/images/2022.07.03/18-Detail.jpg\"  border=\"4pt\">\n          </img>\n        </center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>Credit: Sefaria.org.</center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n  <p>\n                    The accent under the nun has a distinct northeast to southwest inclination.\n               </p>\n  <p>\n                    The Miqra According to the Masorah (MAM) has a meteg under the nun.\n               </p>\n  <p>\n    <b>\n      <i>Daniel Holman</i>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <p align=\"right\">\n    <b><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Changes/2022.10.19 - Changes/2022.10.19 - Changes.xml?2022.07.03-18\">2022.10.19 - Changes.xml : 2022.07.03-18</a>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"20pt\"  border=\"1pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml?c\">All \"Text is correct relative to LC. Usually this marks a peculiarity of the LC relative to the other Masoretic texts.\" ('c') notes</a></center>\n        </p>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml\">Note index</a></center>\n        </p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n</body></HTML>",
  "Joshua.20.4.13-m.html": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/strict.dtd\"><HTML>\n<!-- \n     Computer generated from NoteMaker[20 Jan 2026]: \n     Changes file: 2022.10.19 - Changes.xml, date: 2022.07.03, number: 19 .\n     Remove this token \"****COMPUTER-GENERATED****\" if you edit this file manually.\n-->\n<head><meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\"/>\n  <title>Joshua 20:4.13</title>\n</head>\n<body background=\"../../Images/Background\">\n  <h1>Joshua 20:4.13</h1>\n  <h2>Accent on ayin might be a merkha. Add note 'm'</h2>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"5pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>\n          <img src=\"../../Changes/2022.10.19 - Changes/images/2022.07.03/19-Detail.jpg\"  border=\"4pt\">\n          </img>\n        </center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>Credit: Sefaria.org.</center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n  <p>\n                    The accent on ayin lacks the northeast to southwest inclination to be a merkha.\n               </p>\n  <p>\n                    The Miqra According to the Masorah (MAM) has a merkha under the ayin.\n               </p>\n  <p>\n    <b>\n      <i>Daniel Holman</i>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <p align=\"right\">\n    <b><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Changes/2022.10.19 - Changes/2022.10.19 - Changes.xml?2022.07.03-19\">2022.10.19 - Changes.xml : 2022.07.03-19</a>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"20pt\"  border=\"1pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml?m\">All \"This meteg is a merkha in other texts.\" ('m') notes</a></center>\n        </p>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml\">Note index</a></center>\n        </p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n</body></HTML>",
  "Joshua.21.12.6-m.html": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/strict.dtd\"><HTML>\n<!-- \n     Computer generated from NoteMaker[20 Jan 2026]: \n     Changes file: 2022.10.19 - Changes.xml, date: 2022.07.03, number: 21 .\n     Remove this token \"****COMPUTER-GENERATED****\" if you edit this file manually.\n-->\n<head><meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\"/>\n  <title>Joshua 21:12.6</title>\n</head>\n<body background=\"../../Images/Background\">\n  <h1>Joshua 21:12.6</h1>\n  <h2>Possible merkha under first nun rather than meteg. Add note 'm'.</h2>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"5pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>\n          <img src=\"../../Changes/2022.10.19 - Changes/images/2022.07.03/21-Detail.jpg\"  border=\"4pt\">\n          </img>\n        </center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>Credit: Sefaria.org.</center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n  <p>\n                  The accent under the first nun lacks the northeast to southwest inclination of a merkha.\n               </p>\n  <p>\n                  The Miqra According to the Masorah (MAM) has a merkha on the first nun.\n               </p>\n  <p>\n    <b>\n      <i>Daniel Holman</i>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <p align=\"right\">\n    <b><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Changes/2022.10.19 - Changes/2022.10.19 - Changes.xml?2022.07.03-21\">2022.10.19 - Changes.xml : 2022.07.03-21</a>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"20pt\"  border=\"1pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml?m\">All \"This meteg is a merkha in other texts.\" ('m') notes</a></center>\n        </p>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml\">Note index</a></center>\n        </p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n</body></HTML>",
  "Joshua.21.43.1-t.html": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/strict.dtd\"><HTML>\n<!-- \n     Computer generated from NoteMaker[20 Jan 2026]: \n     Changes file: 2022.10.19 - Changes.xml, date: 2022.07.03, number: 23 .\n     Remove this token \"****COMPUTER-GENERATED****\" if you edit this file manually.\n-->\n<head><meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\"/>\n  <title>Joshua 21:43.1</title>\n</head>\n<body background=\"../../Images/Background\">\n  <h1>Joshua 21:43.1</h1>\n  <h2>Remove dagesh from yod. Add note 't'.</h2>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"5pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>\n          <img src=\"../../Changes/2022.10.19 - Changes/images/2022.07.03/23-Detail.jpg\"  border=\"4pt\">\n          </img>\n        </center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>Credit: Sefaria.org.</center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n  <p>\n                 The putative dagesh on the yod is very faint and may have been erased. \n                 It is much weaker the dagesh on the following tav.\n               </p>\n  <p>\n                  The Miqra According to the Masorah (MAM) has a dagesh on the yod.\n               </p>\n  <p>\n    <b>\n      <i>Daniel Holman</i>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <p align=\"right\">\n    <b><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Changes/2022.10.19 - Changes/2022.10.19 - Changes.xml?2022.07.03-23\">2022.10.19 - Changes.xml : 2022.07.03-23</a>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"20pt\"  border=\"1pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml?t\">All \"Transcription uncertain\" ('t') notes</a></center>\n        </p>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml\">Note index</a></center>\n        </p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n</body></HTML>",
  "Joshua.21.43.5-c.html": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/strict.dtd\"><HTML>\n<!-- \n     Computer generated from NoteMaker[20 Jan 2026]: \n     Changes file: 2022.10.19 - Changes.xml, date: 2022.07.03, number: 24 .\n     Remove this token \"****COMPUTER-GENERATED****\" if you edit this file manually.\n-->\n<head><meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\"/>\n  <title>Joshua 21:43.5</title>\n</head>\n<body background=\"../../Images/Background\">\n  <h1>Joshua 21:43.5</h1>\n  <h2>Add qadma to kaf. Add note 'c'.</h2>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"5pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>\n          <img src=\"../../Changes/2022.10.19 - Changes/images/2022.07.03/24-Detail.jpg\"  border=\"4pt\">\n          </img>\n        </center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>Credit: Sefaria.org.</center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n  <p>\n                 The image shows a poetic word composed of 3 orthographic words connected by 2 maqafs. \n                 The orthographic word in question is the middle word, כָּל־.\n               </p>\n  <p>\n                 The qadma is faint but well-formed. \n                 The aleph on the preceding orthographic word has no accent, the aleph on the following orthographic word has a zaqef qatan.\n               </p>\n  <p>\n                  The Miqra According to the Masorah (MAM) has a qadma on the initial aleph and a zaqef qatan on the second aleph of this poetic word.\n               </p>\n  <p>\n    <b>\n      <i>Daniel Holman</i>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <p align=\"right\">\n    <b><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Changes/2022.10.19 - Changes/2022.10.19 - Changes.xml?2022.07.03-24\">2022.10.19 - Changes.xml : 2022.07.03-24</a>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"20pt\"  border=\"1pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml?c\">All \"Text is correct relative to LC. Usually this marks a peculiarity of the LC relative to the other Masoretic texts.\" ('c') notes</a></center>\n        </p>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml\">Note index</a></center>\n        </p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n</body></HTML>",
  "Joshua.22.7.13-q.html": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/strict.dtd\"><HTML>\n<!-- \n     Computer generated from NoteMaker[20 Jan 2026]: \n     Changes file: 2024.10.19 - Changes.xml, date: 2024.04.15, number: 4 .\n     Remove this token \"****COMPUTER-GENERATED****\" if you edit this file manually.\n-->\n<head><meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\"/>\n  <title>Joshua 22:7.13</title>\n</head>\n<body background=\"../../Images/Background\">\n  <h1>Joshua 22:7.13</h1>\n  <h2>Remove unsupported dagesh from bet in qere word. Add note 'q'. [בְּעֵ֥בֶר]</h2>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"5pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>\n          <img src=\"../../Changes/2024.10.19 - Changes/images/2024.04.15/4-Detail.jpg\"  border=\"4pt\">\n          </img>\n        </center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>Credit: Sefaria.org.</center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n  <p>The qere letters in the right margin (בעבר) replace the mem of the ketiv body text with a bet. The mem does not contain a dagesh in the body text; thus, the bet should not contain a dagesh. This action is the reverse of that on the following Josh 24:15.21. Add note 'q'.</p>\n  <p>BHL has a dagesh in the bet, בְּעֵ֥בֶר.  BHLA has no dagesh in the bet of this word, בְעֵ֥בֶר.</p>\n  <p>\n    <b>\n      <i>CVK</i>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <p align=\"right\">\n    <b><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Changes/2024.10.19 - Changes/2024.10.19 - Changes.xml?2024.04.15-4\">2024.10.19 - Changes.xml : 2024.04.15-4</a>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"20pt\"  border=\"1pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml?q\">All \"UXLC differs from the conventional word for the qere.\" ('q') notes</a></center>\n        </p>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml\">Note index</a></center>\n        </p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n</body></HTML>",
  "Joshua.3.14.9-m.html": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/strict.dtd\"><HTML>\n<!-- \n     Computer generated from NoteMaker[20 Jan 2026]: \n     Changes file: 2022.10.19 - Changes.xml, date: 2022.07.03, number: 5 .\n     Remove this token \"****COMPUTER-GENERATED****\" if you edit this file manually.\n-->\n<head><meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\"/>\n  <title>Joshua 3:14.9</title>\n</head>\n<body background=\"../../Images/Background\">\n  <h1>Joshua 3:14.9</h1>\n  <h2>The meteg belonging to the nun might be a merkha, but is not sufficiently inclined. Add note 'm'.</h2>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"5pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>\n          <img src=\"../../Changes/2022.10.19 - Changes/images/2022.07.03/5-Detail.jpg\"  border=\"4pt\">\n          </img>\n        </center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>Credit: Sefaria.org.</center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n  <p>\n                  The possible merkha under the nun-gimel space is not as inclined northeast to southwest as the following tevir \n                       and appears perpendicular to the base of the nun.\n                </p>\n  <p>\n                    The Miqra According to the Masorah (MAM) has a merkha under the nun.\n               </p>\n  <p>\n    <b>\n      <i>Daniel Holman</i>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <p align=\"right\">\n    <b><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Changes/2022.10.19 - Changes/2022.10.19 - Changes.xml?2022.07.03-5\">2022.10.19 - Changes.xml : 2022.07.03-5</a>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"20pt\"  border=\"1pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml?m\">All \"This meteg is a merkha in other texts.\" ('m') notes</a></center>\n        </p>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml\">Note index</a></center>\n        </p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n</body></HTML>",
  "Joshua.8.15.1-m.html": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/strict.dtd\"><HTML>\n<!-- \n     Computer generated from NoteMaker[20 Jan 2026]: \n     Changes file: 2022.10.19 - Changes.xml, date: 2022.07.03, number: 7 .\n     Remove this token \"****COMPUTER-GENERATED****\" if you edit this file manually.\n-->\n<head><meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\"/>\n  <title>Joshua 8:15.1</title>\n</head>\n<body background=\"../../Images/Background\">\n  <h1>Joshua 8:15.1</h1>\n  <h2>The meteg belonging to the nun might be a merkha, but is not sufficiently inclined. Add note 'm'.</h2>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"5pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>\n          <img src=\"../../Changes/2022.10.19 - Changes/images/2022.07.03/7-Detail.jpg\"  border=\"4pt\">\n          </img>\n        </center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>Credit: Sefaria.org.</center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n  <p>\n                  The possible merkha under the nun-gimel space is not as inclined northeast to southwest as the following tevir.\n                </p>\n  <p>\n                    The Miqra According to the Masorah (MAM) has a merkha under the nun.\n               </p>\n  <p>\n    <b>\n      <i>Daniel Holman</i>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <p align=\"right\">\n    <b><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Changes/2022.10.19 - Changes/2022.10.19 - Changes.xml?2022.07.03-7\">2022.10.19 - Changes.xml : 2022.07.03-7</a>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"20pt\"  border=\"1pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml?m\">All \"This meteg is a merkha in other texts.\" ('m') notes</a></center>\n        </p>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml\">Note index</a></center>\n        </p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n</body></HTML>"
}
